    "created_at": "2019-06-19T00:23:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-19T00:23:15Z",
    "body": "> By that, you mean autofocus would only work in the top-level browsing context? Is that actually true in the existing browsers?\r\n\r\nNo, I wanted to mean that elements with autofocus attribute in all sub-frames should be queued to the top-level queue in order to avoid race between frames.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
